      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.1 Web Architecture"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Web Architecture forms the foundational framework enabling client-server communication across distributed networks.",
        "HTTP Protocol is a stateless, application-layer communication protocol underlying data exchange on the Web.",
        "HTTP Status Codes indicate whether a specific HTTP request has been successfully completed, redirected, or encountered an error.",
        "REST, GraphQL, and gRPC represent distinct architectural paradigms for building modern web APIs.",
        "OWASP Top 10 details the most critical security vulnerabilities affecting contemporary web applications."
      ],
      "id": "ibq679z"
    },
