            "<p><strong>Architecture</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Monolithic</p>",
            "<p>Single deployable unit; all features in one application; tightly coupled</p>",
            "<p>Traditional banking core systems, ERP systems</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SOA (Service-Oriented Architecture)</p>",
            "<p>Loosely coupled services; communicate over enterprise bus (ESB)</p>",
            "<p>Enterprise integration; legacy bank modernisation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Microservices</p>",
            "<p>Small independent services; each with own DB; communicate via API</p>",
            "<p>Netflix, Amazon, modern cloud-native banking apps</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Serverless</p>",
            "<p>Event-driven functions; no server management; scale to zero</p>",
            "<p>Notification services, batch jobs, webhooks</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Event-Driven Architecture</p>",
            "<p>Services communicate via events; decoupled; async</p>",
            "<p>Real-time fraud detection, payment processing, IoT</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation)</p>",
            "<p>Separate read and write models</p>",
            "<p>High-scale systems; financial ledger systems</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Event Sourcing</p>",
            "<p>Store events (not current state); rebuild state from events</p>",
            "<p>Audit trails, banking transaction history</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
